            <ArticleTitle>[A man with chest pain and dyspnoea].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>A8275</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 60-year-old man presented with acute chest pain and dyspnoea, which was caused by pericarditis secondary to a neo-oesophago-pericardial fistula after previous oesophagectomy for oesophageal cancer. The fistula presumably originated from a penetrating peptic ulcer.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
